            <div xml:id="d124">

                <pb facs="0177" n="167" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg167"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/9–1348</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of Defense</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Forrestal</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-09-13">13 September 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: There is forwarded, for your
                    information, a copy of a memorandum to me from the Joint Chiefs of Staff, dated
                    9 September 1948, and entitled “Military Aid for Chinese Armies”. I have
                    forwarded this memorandum to the Secretaries of Army, Navy and Air Force with
                    the request that they proceed in conformity with the recommendations set forth
                    therein.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James Forrestal</hi></signed></closer>





